    "No filesystem destination confinement of same-UID programs: aliasing, symlinking or redirecting gate-local roots or targets into coordinator state is outside the trusted-writer envelope, including explicit TMPDIR redirection.",
    "Pre-existing ambient environment (except D5 activation/readiness inputs and refused gate-local root overrides), user/system/repository Git configuration, shell startup files and other tools configuration are outside the trusted-writer envelope when supplied outside D5 and written by no admitted program. Their effects are not claimed safe. Configuration created, modified or selected by admitted programs, or derived from tracked files, plan.json, coordinator state or CLI arguments remains in scope.",
    "No every-caller closure for coordinator-state writers; no coverage of explicit interpreter launches of non-guarded modules, imported callables, new selectors or omitted launchers. Repository-wide closure and configuration-independent OS confinement belong to U4.9 (OD4).",
    "AST detection covers canonical if __name__ == \"__main__\": comparisons, including reversed operands and equality chains, but misses compound Boolean and other non-canonical guards. Those and entry-point completeness belong to U4.9. Executable-bit scanning is also limited; launchers are a curated claim.",
    "Process exit or signal is not outcome proof; DESIGNATED_BOOTSTRAPS remains empty."
